{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.13.15","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"none","dataSources":[{"sourceType":"competition","sourceId":149921},{"sourceType":"datasetVersion","sourceId":20645374},{"sourceType":"datasetVersion","sourceId":20795968},{"sourceType":"datasetVersion","sourceId":20796617}],"isInternetEnabled":false,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":false}},"nbformat_minor":5,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"id":"cd8591c5","cell_type":"markdown","source":"# GEMMA-FORGE V2: benchmark-driven Gemma 4 Developer Agent submission builder\n\nCompetition-oriented notebook with optional PEFT LoRA packaging, harness-gated evaluation, and reproducibility checks. One notebook that (1) **builds a valid `submission.zip` without needing the harness**, (2) optionally **measures** prompt variants on the official harness with strict validity gates, and (3) only ships the more complex variant if the evidence supports it.\n\n## What was kept from each earlier notebook, and what was dropped\n\n| Source | Kept | Dropped, and why |\n|---|---|---|\n| FORGE-STOP / FORGE-AR | Ignore PR-template boilerplate; budget rule \"at ~5 calls left stop exploring, patch, submit\"; graph neighbours are evidence, not authority; structural validator; optional read-only analyzer sub-agent; strict validity gate and paired McNemar test; offline localization lab | 7-class failure ledger and utility formula `U(a)` (long prompt for a small model, no evidence it helps); graph propagation (measured neutral at small beta, harmful at beta 1.0) |\n| ECHO | `search_similar_code` takes **symbol names**, not sentences; at most 3 competing hypotheses; only tool output counts as evidence; never repeat an identical failed action | Mandatory 3-4 hypothesis table on every task (context cost); self-imposed 22 calls / 4 min budget |\n| CIG-HGP + DP-VR | Localize first (aim for about 8 calls), then smallest edit, then verify (syntax check, narrowest test, diff check); scratch files only in `/tmp` | Custom AST/PageRank script run through `run_command` (costs paid calls, unvalidated `skills:` key); unverified `{problem_description}` placeholders |\n| New here | Mirrors the **official sample submission's** `eval_config.yaml` instead of guessing budgets; fixes the earlier crashes (`swegemma` path `None`, `pip` failing on `google-cloud-aiplatform`); marks Docker/infra failures as INVALID, never as a zero score | |\n\n## Honest status\nThis is a prompt-and-config agent. It does not train adapters. Nothing in this notebook claims a pass rate. The decision about which arm to submit is made by the paired comparison in section 8, and defaults to the lean arm if no valid run exists.\n\n## V2 changes\n- Archive-aware snapshot lookup for `.tgz`, `.tar.gz`, and `.tar` snapshots.\n- Safe extraction: reject traversal paths and skip links/special archive entries.\n- Correct optional LoRA YAML formatting and package adapter files under `adapters/<name>/`.\n- Add an analyzer + LoRA evaluation arm when a compatible adapter is provided.\n- Compare candidates against the official sample and export `benchmark_results.csv`.\n- Local benchmark results are diagnostic, not hidden leaderboard scores.\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"a42f42d2","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## How to run on Kaggle\n1. Attach the competition data, the wheelhouse dataset and the Gemma 4 31B model. Internet **off**. Accelerator: 4×L4.\n2. Run sections 0-6 top to bottom. That produces `/kaggle/working/submission.zip`. Snapshot archives are extracted lazily for the optional localization lab.\n3. Section 7-9 (harness evaluation) run only if Docker and `swegemma` are available. If they are not, the notebook says so and skips them; it does not fake results.\n4. Before uploading, read the checklist in section 10.","metadata":{}},{"id":"e0abb7ab","cell_type":"code","source":"# 0. Setup and path discovery (all paths overridable through environment variables)\nimport os, sys, json, re, math, time, shutil, hashlib, zipfile, subprocess, random, platform\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\n\nMODEL_ID = os.environ.get(\"GEMMA_MODEL_ID\", \"gemma-4-31b-it-qat-w4a16-ct\")\nINPUT = Path(os.environ.get(\"GEMMA_INPUT\", \"/kaggle/input\"))\nWORK = Path(os.environ.get(\"GEMMA_WORK\", \"/kaggle/working\"))\nWORK.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\nSEED = 2026\nrandom.seed(SEED)\n\ndef find_comp_root():\n    env = os.environ.get(\"GEMMA_COMP_DIR\")\n    if env:\n        return Path(env)\n    for p in (INPUT / \"competitions\" / \"gemma-4-developer-agent\", INPUT / \"gemma-4-developer-agent\"):\n        if (p / \"tasks.jsonl\").is_file():\n            return p\n    for pat in (\"*/tasks.jsonl\", \"*/*/tasks.jsonl\", \"*/*/*/tasks.jsonl\"):   # shallow search only\n        for p in INPUT.glob(pat):\n            return p.parent\n    return None\n\ndef find_wheelhouse():\n    env = os.environ.get(\"GEMMA_WHEELHOUSE\")\n    if env:\n        return Path(env)\n    for p in (INPUT / \"datasets/metric/gemma-4-developer-agent-wheelhouse\", INPUT / \"gemma-4-developer-agent-wheelhouse\"):\n        if p.is_dir():\n            return p\n    for pat in (\"*/swegemma-*.whl\", \"*/*/swegemma-*.whl\", \"*/*/*/swegemma-*.whl\"):\n        for p in INPUT.glob(pat):\n            return p.parent\n    return None\n\nCOMP = find_comp_root()\nWHEELHOUSE = find_wheelhouse()\nTASKS_PATH = COMP / \"tasks.jsonl\" if COMP else None\nSNAPSHOTS = (COMP / \"snapshots\") if COMP and (COMP / \"snapshots\").is_dir() else None\nSAMPLE_SUB = (COMP / \"sample_submission\") if COMP and (COMP / \"sample_submission\").is_dir() else None\nARMS_DIR = WORK / \"arms\"\nRESULTS_DIR = WORK / \"eval_runs\"\n\n# Tunables. Sampling values are reasoned defaults, NOT tuned. The 32K context window is shared with thinking.\nMAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS = int(os.environ.get(\"GEMMA_MAX_OUTPUT\", \"8192\"))\nTHINKING_BUDGET = int(os.environ.get(\"GEMMA_THINKING\", \"3072\"))\nTEMPERATURE, TOP_P = 0.2, 0.95\n\n# Optional PEFT adapter: point GEMMA_LORA_DIR to a trained adapter directory.\n# Keep disabled for the baseline. The harness README permits safetensors adapters only.\nLORA_DIR = Path(os.environ[\"GEMMA_LORA_DIR\"]) if os.environ.get(\"GEMMA_LORA_DIR\") else None\nLORA_NAME = os.environ.get(\"GEMMA_LORA_NAME\", \"forge_lora\")\nUSE_LORA = bool(LORA_DIR and LORA_DIR.is_dir())\nif USE_LORA:\n    required_lora = (\"adapter_config.json\", \"adapter_model.safetensors\")\n    missing_lora = [name for name in required_lora if not (LORA_DIR / name).is_file()]\n    if missing_lora:\n        raise FileNotFoundError(f\"GEMMA_LORA_DIR is missing required PEFT files: {missing_lora}\")\n    adapter_cfg = json.loads((LORA_DIR / \"adapter_config.json\").read_text())\n    LORA_RANK = int(adapter_cfg.get(\"r\", 0))\n    if not 1 <= LORA_RANK <= 128:\n        raise ValueError(f\"LoRA rank {LORA_RANK} is outside harness-supported 1..128\")\n    if adapter_cfg.get(\"base_model_name_or_path\") and MODEL_ID not in adapter_cfg[\"base_model_name_or_path\"]:\n        print(\"WARNING: adapter base_model_name_or_path differs from MODEL_ID; verify compatibility.\")\nelse:\n    LORA_RANK = None\nprint(\"LoRA adapter:\", f\"{LORA_NAME} (rank={LORA_RANK})\" if USE_LORA else \"disabled (base model)\")\n\nprint(\"model        :\", MODEL_ID)\nprint(\"competition  :\", COMP)\nprint(\"tasks.jsonl  :\", TASKS_PATH, \"| exists:\", bool(TASKS_PATH and TASKS_PATH.is_file()))\nprint(\"snapshots    :\", SNAPSHOTS)\nprint(\"sample sub   :\", SAMPLE_SUB)\nprint(\"wheelhouse   :\", WHEELHOUSE)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-07T04:48:30.918563Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-07T04:48:30.918958Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-07T04:48:30.939847Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-07T04:48:30.918927Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-07T04:48:30.938882Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"LoRA adapter: disabled (base model)\nmodel        : gemma-4-31b-it-qat-w4a16-ct\ncompetition  : /kaggle/input/competitions/gemma-4-developer-agent\ntasks.jsonl  : /kaggle/input/competitions/gemma-4-developer-agent/tasks.jsonl | exists: True\nsnapshots    : /kaggle/input/competitions/gemma-4-developer-agent/snapshots\nsample sub   : /kaggle/input/competitions/gemma-4-developer-agent/sample_submission\nwheelhouse   : /kaggle/input/datasets/metric/gemma-4-developer-agent-wheelhouse\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":4},{"id":"c2b8499f","cell_type":"code","source":"# 1. Preflight. Nothing here is required for BUILDING the submission; it only decides whether the harness\n#    evaluation (section 7+) can run. Docker/infra problems are reported, never scored as failed repairs.\ndef sh(cmd, timeout=30):\n    try:\n        p = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=timeout)\n        return p.returncode, (p.stdout or \"\") + (p.stderr or \"\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        return 127, repr(e)\n\nrc, out = sh([\"nvidia-smi\", \"-L\"])\nGPU_COUNT = len([l for l in out.splitlines() if l.startswith(\"GPU \")]) if rc == 0 else 0\nL4_OK = GPU_COUNT == 4 and all(\"L4\" in l for l in out.splitlines() if l.startswith(\"GPU \"))\nrc, out = sh([\"docker\", \"info\", \"--format\", \"{{.ServerVersion}}\"], timeout=20)\nDOCKER_OK = (rc == 0 and out.strip() != \"\")\nDOCKER_MSG = out.strip()[:200]\n\n# Make the pip-installed CLI findable (an earlier notebook crashed because shutil.which() returned None).\nos.environ[\"PATH\"] = str(Path(sys.executable).parent) + os.pathsep + \"/usr/local/bin\" + os.pathsep + os.environ.get(\"PATH\", \"\")\nSWEGEMMA = shutil.which(\"swegemma\")\n\nINSTALL_HARNESS = os.environ.get(\"GEMMA_INSTALL_HARNESS\", \"0\") == \"1\"\nif not SWEGEMMA and INSTALL_HARNESS and WHEELHOUSE:\n    # --no-deps: an earlier run failed because pip tried to resolve google-cloud-aiplatform, which is not in the wheelhouse.\n    wheels = [str(next(iter(sorted(WHEELHOUSE.glob(f\"{n}-*.whl\"))), \"\")) for n in (\"swegemma\", \"adk_eval_core\", \"adk_submission\")]\n    wheels = [w for w in wheels if w]\n    rc, out = sh([sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pip\", \"install\", \"--no-index\", \"--no-deps\", *wheels], timeout=300)\n    print(\"wheel install rc =\", rc, out[-800:])\n    SWEGEMMA = shutil.which(\"swegemma\")\n\nprint(f\"GPUs visible : {GPU_COUNT}  (4xL4 verified: {L4_OK})\")\nprint(f\"Docker       : {'OK ' + DOCKER_MSG if DOCKER_OK else 'NOT AVAILABLE -> ' + DOCKER_MSG}\")\nprint(f\"swegemma CLI : {SWEGEMMA}\")\nCAN_RUN_HARNESS = bool(SWEGEMMA and DOCKER_OK and TASKS_PATH and SNAPSHOTS and SAMPLE_SUB)\nprint(\"Harness evaluation possible:\", CAN_RUN_HARNESS)\nif not CAN_RUN_HARNESS:\n    print(\"-> Packaging (sections 0-6) still works. Sections 7-9 will be skipped.\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-07T04:48:30.941423Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-07T04:48:30.941957Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-07T04:48:30.967931Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-07T04:48:30.941929Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-07T04:48:30.966756Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"GPUs visible : 0  (4xL4 verified: False)\nDocker       : NOT AVAILABLE -> FileNotFoundError(2, 'No such file or directory')\nswegemma CLI : None\nHarness evaluation possible: False\n-> Packaging (sections 0-6) still works. Sections 7-9 will be skipped.\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":5},{"id":"de8154f6","cell_type":"code","source":"# 2. Load tasks and inspect the OFFICIAL sample submission (the only known-good reference for format and budgets).\nTASKS = []\nif TASKS_PATH and TASKS_PATH.is_file():\n    with TASKS_PATH.open(encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        for line in f:\n            if line.strip():\n                TASKS.append(json.loads(line))\n    print(\"tasks:\", len(TASKS), \"| repos:\", dict(Counter(t.get(\"repo\") for t in TASKS)))\nelse:\n    print(\"No tasks.jsonl found; the localization lab and harness runs will be skipped.\")\n\nFALLBACK_BUDGET = dict(max_tool_calls=100, max_time_minutes=60, max_turns=500, timeout_seconds=600)\nBUDGET = dict(FALLBACK_BUDGET)\nBUDGET_SOURCE = \"FALLBACK (values used by the FORGE notebooks; confirm in HARNESS_README.md)\"\nSAMPLE_PLACEHOLDERS = []\n\nif SAMPLE_SUB:\n    print(\"\\nsample_submission files:\", sorted(str(p.relative_to(SAMPLE_SUB)) for p in SAMPLE_SUB.rglob(\"*\") if p.is_file())[:30])\n    ay = next((SAMPLE_SUB / n for n in (\"agent.yaml\", \"agent.yml\", \"root_agent.yaml\") if (SAMPLE_SUB / n).exists()), None)\n    if ay:\n        print(\"\\n--- sample agent.yaml (first 1500 chars) ---\\n\" + ay.read_text()[:1500])\n    ec = SAMPLE_SUB / \"eval_config.yaml\"\n    if ec.exists():\n        txt = ec.read_text()\n        print(\"\\n--- sample eval_config.yaml ---\\n\" + txt)\n        for k in BUDGET:\n            m = re.search(rf\"{k}:\\s*(\\d+)\", txt)\n            if m:\n                BUDGET[k] = int(m.group(1))\n        BUDGET_SOURCE = \"mirrored from sample_submission/eval_config.yaml\"\n    for p in SAMPLE_SUB.rglob(\"*.md\"):\n        SAMPLE_PLACEHOLDERS += re.findall(r\"\\{[a-zA-Z_]+\\}\", p.read_text(errors=\"replace\"))\n    print(\"\\nplaceholders used by the sample's prompts:\", sorted(set(SAMPLE_PLACEHOLDERS)) or \"none\")\nprint(\"\\nBUDGET:\", BUDGET, \"|\", BUDGET_SOURCE)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-07T04:48:30.969474Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-07T04:48:30.969926Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-07T04:48:31.058172Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-07T04:48:30.969878Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-07T04:48:31.057287Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"tasks: 129 | repos: {'fastapi/fastapi': 67, 'psf/requests': 13, 'Textualize/rich': 48, 'encode/httpx': 1}\n\nsample_submission files: ['adapters/main_lora/adapter_config.json', 'adapters/main_lora/adapter_model.safetensors', 'adapters/tool_lora/adapter_config.json', 'adapters/tool_lora/adapter_model.safetensors', 'agent.yaml', 'configs/sampling.yaml', 'eval_config.yaml', 'prompts/analyzer.md', 'prompts/system.md', 'sub_agents/code_analyzer.yaml']\n\n--- sample agent.yaml (first 1500 chars) ---\nname: swe_baseline_agent\nmodel: gemma-4-31b-it-qat-w4a16-ct\nadapter: main_lora\ninstruction: !include prompts/system.md\ntools:\n  - run_command\n  - read_file\n  - edit_file\n  - write_file\n  - get_status\n  - submit_patch\n  - get_code_neighbors\n  - search_similar_code\n  - get_code_subgraph\n  - agent_tool:\n      config_path: sub_agents/code_analyzer.yaml\n      skip_summarization: true\ngenerate_content_config: !include configs/sampling.yaml\n\n\n--- sample eval_config.yaml ---\n# Optional participant evaluation configuration for Stage 1 inference.\n# Controls per-task execution budgets and sandbox command timeouts.\nevaluation:\n  timeout_seconds: 60\n  max_tool_calls: 10\n  max_time_minutes: 1\n  max_turns: 50\n\n\nplaceholders used by the sample's prompts: none\n\nBUDGET: {'max_tool_calls': 10, 'max_time_minutes': 1, 'max_turns': 50, 'timeout_seconds': 60} | mirrored from sample_submission/eval_config.yaml\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":6},{"id":"db448625","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 3. Offline localization lab (CPU, optional)\n\nPurpose: check cheaply, **before** spending GPU time, whether the prompt's advice about the task text is sound. The FORGE notebooks found that stripping pull-request boilerplate from the query was the largest single localization gain (unit MRR 0.221 to 0.347 across the chain). This compact lab re-tests that idea at **file level**: how high does a BM25 + identifier ranker put the files that the gold patch changed, with and without query cleaning?\n\nIt uses the gold `patch` field **only to score** and never puts it in the agent's prompt or submission. It is a diagnostic, not a pass rate.","metadata":{}},{"id":"ad0c83c0","cell_type":"code","source":"# 3a. Compact localization library (stdlib only)\nimport ast, tarfile\n\nSKIP_DIRS = {\".git\", \".venv\", \"venv\", \"__pycache__\", \".tox\", \"build\", \"dist\", \".pytest_cache\", \"node_modules\", \"docs\", \"docs_src\", \"examples\"}\nSTOP = set(\"the and for with from this that when where what which have has into then than there their should would could does not are was were been being issue error test failed failure expected actual line file traceback python self none true false return import\".split())\n\n_BOILER = [\n    (re.compile(r\"<!--.*?-->\", re.S), \" \"),                                   # HTML comments (PR templates)\n    (re.compile(r\"^\\s*[-*]\\s*\\[[ xX]\\].*$\", re.M), \" \"),                        # checklists\n    (re.compile(r\"https?://\\S+\"), \" \"),                                         # URLs\n    (re.compile(r\"\\b(?:fix(?:es|ed)?|close[sd]?|resolve[sd]?)\\s+#\\d+\", re.I), \" \"),\n    (re.compile(r\"(?<!\\w)#\\d+\\b\"), \" \"),                                        # issue numbers\n    (re.compile(r\"^\\s*#{1,6}\\s*\", re.M), \"\"),                                   # markdown heading marks\n]\ndef clean_query(text):\n    for pat, rep in _BOILER:\n        text = pat.sub(rep, text or \"\")\n    return re.sub(r\"\\s+\", \" \", text).strip()\n\ndef extract_idents(text):\n    ids = set()\n    ids |= {m.strip().lower() for m in re.findall(r\"`([A-Za-z_][\\w\\.]{2,})`\", text or \"\")}\n    ids |= {m.lower() for m in re.findall(r\"\\b[A-Z][a-z0-9]+(?:[A-Z][a-z0-9]+)+\\b\", text or \"\")}   # CamelCase\n    ids |= {m.lower() for m in re.findall(r\"\\b[a-z]+_[a-z0-9_]+\\b\", text or \"\")}                  # snake_case\n    out = set()\n    for i in ids:\n        out.add(i)\n        out |= {p for p in i.split(\".\") if len(p) > 2}\n    return {i for i in out if i not in STOP}\n\ndef tokenize(s):\n    s = re.sub(r\"([a-z0-9])([A-Z])\", r\"\\1 \\2\", s or \"\")\n    return [w for w in re.findall(r\"[a-z]{2,}\", s.lower()) if w not in STOP]\n\ndef is_test_path(p):\n    parts = p.lower().split(\"/\")\n    name = parts[-1]\n    return any(x in (\"tests\", \"test\", \"testing\") for x in parts[:-1]) or name.startswith(\"test_\") or name.endswith(\"_test.py\") or name == \"conftest.py\"\n\nclass RepoIndex:\n    def __init__(self, root, max_files=3000):\n        self.docs = []   # (relpath, Counter, length, names_lower, path_lower)\n        df = Counter()\n        n = 0\n        for p in Path(root).rglob(\"*.py\"):\n            rel = p.relative_to(root).as_posix()\n            if any(x in SKIP_DIRS for x in p.relative_to(root).parts) or is_test_path(rel):\n                continue\n            try:\n                if p.stat().st_size > 400_000:\n                    continue\n                src = p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n            except OSError:\n                continue\n            names = set()\n            try:\n                for node in ast.walk(ast.parse(src)):\n                    if isinstance(node, (ast.FunctionDef, ast.AsyncFunctionDef, ast.ClassDef)):\n                        names.add(node.name.lower())\n            except Exception:\n                pass\n            toks = tokenize(rel) * 3 + tokenize(\" \".join(names)) * 2 + tokenize(src[:8000])\n            c = Counter(toks)\n            self.docs.append((rel, c, max(1, len(toks)), names, rel.lower()))\n            df.update(c.keys())\n            n += 1\n            if n >= max_files:\n                break\n        self.N = max(1, len(self.docs))\n        self.df = df\n        self.avgdl = sum(d[2] for d in self.docs) / self.N\n\n    def rank(self, query, idents=None, k1=1.2, b=0.75, id_weight=0.15):\n        q = tokenize(query)\n        scores = []\n        for rel, c, dl, names, pl in self.docs:\n            s = 0.0\n            for t in set(q):\n                f = c.get(t, 0)\n                if f:\n                    idf = math.log(1 + (self.N - self.df[t] + 0.5) / (self.df[t] + 0.5))\n                    s += idf * f * (k1 + 1) / (f + k1 * (1 - b + b * dl / self.avgdl))\n            scores.append(s)\n        mx = max(scores) if scores and max(scores) > 0 else 1.0\n        final = []\n        for (rel, c, dl, names, pl), s in zip(self.docs, scores):\n            bonus = 0.0\n            for i in (idents or ()):\n                if i in names:\n                    bonus += 1.0\n                elif len(i) > 3 and i in pl:\n                    bonus += 0.6\n            final.append((s / mx + id_weight * min(bonus, 4.0), rel))\n        final.sort(reverse=True)\n        return [rel for _, rel in final]\n\ndef gold_files(patch):\n    files = re.findall(r\"^diff --git a/(\\S+) b/\\S+\", patch or \"\", re.M)\n    return [f for f in dict.fromkeys(files) if f.endswith(\".py\") and not is_test_path(f)]\n\nSNAPSHOT_CACHE = WORK / \"snapshot_cache\"\nSNAPSHOT_CACHE.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\ndef _safe_extract_tar(archive, destination):\n    \"\"\"Extract regular files/directories only; reject traversal and ignore links.\"\"\"\n    destination = Path(destination).resolve()\n    destination.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    with tarfile.open(archive, \"r:*\") as tf:\n        for member in tf.getmembers():\n            rel = Path(member.name)\n            if rel.is_absolute() or \"..\" in rel.parts:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Unsafe archive member path: {member.name}\")\n            target = (destination / rel).resolve()\n            if target != destination and destination not in target.parents:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Archive member escapes extraction root: {member.name}\")\n            if member.isdir():\n                target.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n            elif member.isfile():\n                target.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n                stream = tf.extractfile(member)\n                if stream is not None:\n                    with stream, target.open(\"wb\") as dst:\n                        shutil.copyfileobj(stream, dst)\n            # Symlinks, hardlinks, devices and special entries are skipped.\n\ndef _snapshot_archives(iid, task):\n    candidates = []\n    for key in (\"snapshot\", \"snapshot_path\", \"archive\", \"archive_path\"):\n        value = task.get(key)\n        if value:\n            p = Path(value)\n            candidates.append(p if p.is_absolute() else SNAPSHOTS / p)\n    for suffix in (\".tgz\", \".tar.gz\", \".tar\"):\n        candidates.extend((SNAPSHOTS / f\"{iid}{suffix}\", SNAPSHOTS / iid / f\"repo{suffix}\"))\n    candidates.extend(p for p in SNAPSHOTS.glob(f\"{iid}*.t*\")\n                      if p.is_file() and p.suffix in (\".tgz\", \".gz\", \".tar\"))\n    seen = set()\n    for p in candidates:\n        try:\n            key = p.resolve()\n        except Exception:\n            continue\n        if key not in seen and p.is_file():\n            seen.add(key)\n            yield p\n\ndef locate_snapshot(task):\n    iid = task.get(\"instance_id\")\n    if SNAPSHOTS is None or not iid:\n        return None\n    for cand in (SNAPSHOTS / iid, SNAPSHOTS / iid / \"repo\",\n                 SNAPSHOTS / iid / \"workspace\", SNAPSHOTS / iid / \"src\"):\n        if cand.is_dir() and any(cand.rglob(\"*.py\")):\n            return cand\n\n    cache_dir = SNAPSHOT_CACHE / re.sub(r\"[^A-Za-z0-9_.-]\", \"_\", iid)\n    marker = cache_dir / \".gemma_forge_extracted\"\n    if not marker.exists():\n        archive = next(iter(_snapshot_archives(iid, task)), None)\n        if archive is None:\n            return None\n        shutil.rmtree(cache_dir, ignore_errors=True)\n        cache_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        try:\n            _safe_extract_tar(archive, cache_dir)\n            marker.write_text(str(archive), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        except Exception as exc:\n            shutil.rmtree(cache_dir, ignore_errors=True)\n            print(f\"Snapshot archive skipped for {iid}: {exc}\")\n            return None\n    if not any(p.is_file() for p in cache_dir.rglob(\"*.py\")):\n        return None\n    return cache_dir\n\ndef metrics(rank_lists, golds):\n    out = {\"n\": 0, \"acc@1\": 0, \"acc@3\": 0, \"acc@5\": 0, \"acc@10\": 0, \"mrr\": 0.0}\n    per = []\n    for ranks, gold in zip(rank_lists, golds):\n        pos = [i + 1 for i, r in enumerate(ranks) if r in gold]\n        r1 = min(pos) if pos else None\n        out[\"n\"] += 1\n        for k in (1, 3, 5, 10):\n            out[f\"acc@{k}\"] += int(r1 is not None and r1 <= k)\n        rr = 1.0 / r1 if r1 else 0.0\n        out[\"mrr\"] += rr\n        per.append(rr)\n    n = max(1, out[\"n\"])\n    for k in out:\n        if k != \"n\":\n            out[k] = round(out[k] / n, 3)\n    return out, per\nprint(\"lab library ready\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-07T04:48:31.116277Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-07T04:48:31.116806Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-07T04:48:31.160007Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-07T04:48:31.11677Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-07T04:48:31.159032Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"lab library ready\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":7},{"id":"d0ac5799","cell_type":"code","source":"# 3b. Run the lab. Skipped automatically when snapshots or tasks are missing.\nLAB_MAX = int(os.environ.get(\"GEMMA_LAB_MAX\", \"0\")) or None     # e.g. GEMMA_LAB_MAX=40 for a quick run\nLAB = {}\nif TASKS and SNAPSHOTS:\n    import pandas as pd\n    rows, found, missing = [], 0, 0\n    use = TASKS[:LAB_MAX] if LAB_MAX else TASKS\n    t0 = time.time()\n    for t in use:\n        gold = set(gold_files(t.get(\"patch\", \"\")))\n        snap = locate_snapshot(t)\n        if not gold:\n            continue\n        if snap is None:\n            missing += 1\n            continue\n        found += 1\n        idx = RepoIndex(snap)\n        raw, cln = t.get(\"problem_statement\", \"\"), clean_query(t.get(\"problem_statement\", \"\"))\n        rows.append(dict(\n            repo=t.get(\"repo\"), gold=gold,\n            raw=idx.rank(raw), cleaned=idx.rank(cln),\n            cleaned_ids=idx.rank(cln, extract_idents(t.get(\"problem_statement\", \"\")))))\n    print(f\"scored {found} tasks ({missing} had no locatable snapshot dir) in {time.time()-t0:.0f}s\")\n    if found == 0 and SNAPSHOTS.exists():\n        print(\"Snapshot layout not recognised. First entries:\", [p.name for p in list(SNAPSHOTS.iterdir())[:8]],\n              \"-> adjust locate_snapshot() if you want the lab; the rest of the notebook is unaffected.\")\n    if rows:\n        table, per_variant = {}, {}\n        for name, label in ((\"raw\", \"raw issue text\"), (\"cleaned\", \"cleaned query\"), (\"cleaned_ids\", \"cleaned + identifier bonus\")):\n            m, per = metrics([r[name] for r in rows], [r[\"gold\"] for r in rows])\n            table[label] = m\n            per_variant[name] = per\n        LAB[\"table\"] = pd.DataFrame(table).T\n        print(LAB[\"table\"].to_string())\n        d = [b - a for a, b in zip(per_variant[\"raw\"], per_variant[\"cleaned_ids\"])]\n        print(f\"\\ncleaned+ids vs raw (file MRR): wins={sum(x>0 for x in d)} losses={sum(x<0 for x in d)} ties={sum(x==0 for x in d)}\")\n        LAB[\"cleaning_helps\"] = sum(x > 0 for x in d) > sum(x < 0 for x in d)\n        print(\"File-level diagnostic only; not a pass rate. Use the result to decide whether to keep the cleaning rule in the prompt.\")\nelse:\n    print(\"Lab skipped (needs tasks.jsonl and snapshots/).\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-07T04:48:31.161787Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-07T04:48:31.162225Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-07T04:55:51.377943Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-07T04:48:31.162195Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-07T04:55:51.376816Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Snapshot archive skipped 