ich_4075.tgz', 'fastapi_14791.tgz', 'fastapi_14463.tgz', 'requests_7315.tgz', 'fastapi_13920.tgz', 'rich_3052.tgz', 'requests_6592.tgz'] -> adjust locate_snapshot() if you want the lab; the rest of the notebook is unaffected.\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":8},{"id":"8a1185c2-6b19-45b3-bc74-896189161217","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Competition upgrade notes: harness fidelity + LoRA\n\n- Submission stays **declarative YAML only**; no custom Python entrypoint is introduced.\n- Optional PEFT LoRA is referenced with `adapter:` and packaged only when `adapter_config.json` and `adapter_model.safetensors` exist. Rank is checked ≤128; keep the complete unpacked archive below 3 GiB.\n- This notebook does **not train** an adapter. Train/validate separately against the same base checkpoint, then set `GEMMA_LORA_DIR`. Compare base vs adapter on identical task IDs, after the official sample passes the infrastructure gate.\n- The CPU localization lab is diagnostic only, not a resolution-rate score.\n- The README documents a shared 32K context ceiling; thinking and output tokens both consume it.\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"ea625f21","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 4. Prompt design\n\nThe merged prompt is deliberately short (about 700 words). The 32K context window is shared between the prompt, tool output, and thinking, and the FORGE-AR run itself noted that very long controller prompts are a risk for a small model. Every rule below is one of: a hard harness constraint, a budget guard, or a behaviour all three earlier notebooks agreed on.\n\nThree arms are built so that the extra machinery has to earn its place:\n\n| Arm | Contents |\n|---|---|\n| `M0_minimal` | One-paragraph control prompt. Sanity floor. |\n| `L1_lean` | The merged prompt. **Default submission.** |\n| `L2_lean_analyzer` | `L1_lean` plus a read-only `code_analyzer` sub-agent (from FORGE). Adds delegation overhead, so it ships only if it wins in section 8. |","metadata":{}},{"id":"b2ba10db","cell_type":"code","source":"# 4. Prompts\nLEAN_PROMPT = \"\"\"You are an autonomous software engineer fixing one issue in the repository at /workspace. A hidden test suite checks your patch. The environment is offline: no network, no installs.\n\n## Goal\nMake the smallest correct change to SOURCE code so the behaviour described in the issue is fixed. Never end without a non-empty source patch.\n\n## Workflow\n1. Read the task. It may be a pull-request description with template boilerplate (checklists, HTML comments, disclaimers, links, issue numbers). Ignore that. Extract the symptom, the expected behaviour, exact error messages, exception types, status codes, signatures, and any backticked identifiers. Follow these exactly.\n2. Localize before editing; aim to finish within about 8 paid calls.\n   - search_similar_code takes SYMBOL names such as `Class.method`, not sentences. Query it with identifiers from the issue.\n   - For exact strings (an error message, an option name) use run_command with grep -rn.\n   - get_code_neighbors on the best match shows callers and callees. Treat graph results as evidence, not authority: follow a neighbour only if it agrees with the issue text. Generic helpers and widely used utilities are usually noise; if graph hops lead there, go back to your exact-identifier matches.\n   - Keep at most 3 competing hypotheses (file or symbol, plus what would confirm or refute it). Prefer the cheapest action that separates them. Only tool output counts as evidence; your own guesses do not. Drop refuted hypotheses and never repeat an identical action without new evidence.\n3. Read narrowly: read_file with line ranges around the symbol, the way callers use it, and the nearest existing test.\n4. Edit in small steps: one logical change per edit_file call, a short unique old_string, no whole-file rewrites. Preserve public APIs and repository style. Do not refactor or reformat unrelated code. Never edit tests, conftest.py, pytest.ini, pyproject.toml, tox.ini or setup.cfg (those changes are discarded).\n5. Verify cheaply. Run a syntax or import check, then only the narrowest relevant test (for example pytest path/to/test_x.py -k name -x -q). Never run the whole suite. If something fails, classify it (wrong location, missing symbol or import, syntax or patch error, failing assertion, regression, environment problem), treat the output as new evidence, and make at most one focused correction. For a regression, compare with the pre-edit behaviour, then narrow or revert the last change. Do not call an environment failure a code fix. Never claim a test passed unless the command output shows it.\n6. Finish. Inspect git diff and git status: only intended source files may be changed. Keep scratch scripts in /tmp, never in /workspace. Call submit_patch exactly once as your final tool action, then give a one-line summary.\n\n## Budget\nCall get_status after about every 4th tool call. When 5 or fewer tool calls remain, or time is nearly out, stop exploring: make the best evidence-supported minimal edit, run the cheapest relevant check, inspect the diff, and submit. A good small patch submitted in time beats a perfect patch that never gets submitted.\n\"\"\"\n\nMINIMAL_PROMPT = \"\"\"You are a careful software engineer working inside /workspace. Read the issue, find the relevant source code with the available tools, make a minimal source patch, run the most relevant existing test, check git diff, and call submit_patch exactly once as your last tool action. Do not edit tests or test configuration. The environment is offline.\"\"\"\n\nANALYZER_PROMPT = \"\"\"You are a read-only code analysis sub-agent. Find where the reported issue lives; do not edit anything.\n1. Take identifiers from the issue (class, function, argument, message names) and call search_similar_code with a symbol name such as `Class.method`, then get_code_neighbors on the best match.\n2. Read only the lines you need (read_file).\n3. Reply in at most 150 words, no code blocks: the file:line to change, the root cause in one or two sentences, and the smallest change that fixes it. Say clearly if you are unsure.\"\"\"\n\nest_tokens = lambda s: int(len(s.split()) * 1.35)\nprint(\"approx prompt tokens:\", {\"M0\": est_tokens(MINIMAL_PROMPT), \"L1\": est_tokens(LEAN_PROMPT), \"analyzer\": est_tokens(ANALYZER_PROMPT)})\nassert est_tokens(LEAN_PROMPT) < 1300, \"lean prompt grew too large for a 32K shared context\"\nassert not re.search(r\"\\{[a-zA-Z_]+\\}\", LEAN_PROMPT), \"prompt contains an unfilled {placeholder}\"","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-07T04:55:51.383248Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-07T04:55:51.384081Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-07T04:55:51.397437Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-07T04:55:51.384041Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-07T04:55:51.396366Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"approx prompt tokens: {'M0': 75, 'L1': 662, 'analyzer': 117}\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":9},{"id":"8ed82755","cell_type":"code","source":"# 5. Build the arms. Same structure that the earlier FORGE notebooks validated: !include for prompts and sampling.\nBASE_TOOLS = [\"run_command\", \"read_file\", \"edit_file\", \"write_file\", \"get_status\", \"submit_patch\"]\nGRAPH_TOOLS = [\"get_code_neighbors\", \"search_similar_code\", \"get_code_subgraph\"]\n\nSAMPLING_YAML = (f\"temperature: {TEMPERATURE}\\ntop_p: {TOP_P}\\nmax_output_tokens: {MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS}\\n\"\n                 f\"thinking_config:\\n  include_thoughts: true\\n  thinking_budget: {THINKING_BUDGET}\\n\")\nEVAL_YAML = (\"evaluation:\\n\" + \"\".join(f\"  {k}: {v}\\n\" for k, v in\n             ((\"timeout_seconds\", BUDGET[\"timeout_seconds\"]), (\"max_tool_calls\", BUDGET[\"max_tool_calls\"]),\n              (\"max_time_minutes\", BUDGET[\"max_time_minutes\"]), (\"max_turns\", BUDGET[\"max_turns\"]))))\n\ndef write_arm(name, prompt, analyzer=False, tools=None):\n    d = ARMS_DIR / name\n    shutil.rmtree(d, ignore_errors=True)\n    (d / \"prompts\").mkdir(parents=True)\n    (d / \"configs\").mkdir()\n    (d / \"prompts/system.md\").write_text(prompt.strip() + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    (d / \"configs/sampling.yaml\").write_text(SAMPLING_YAML, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    (d / \"eval_config.yaml\").write_text(EVAL_YAML, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    if USE_LORA:\n        adapter_dst = d / \"adapters\" / LORA_NAME\n        adapter_dst.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        shutil.copy2(LORA_DIR / \"adapter_config.json\", adapter_dst / \"adapter_config.json\")\n        shutil.copy2(LORA_DIR / \"adapter_model.safetensors\", adapter_dst / \"adapter_model.safetensors\")\n    tools = tools or (BASE_TOOLS + GRAPH_TOOLS)\n    adapter_line = f\"adapter: {LORA_NAME}\\n\" if USE_LORA else \"\"\n    y = f\"name: {re.sub(r'[^a-zA-Z0-9_]', '_', name).lower()}\\nmodel: {MODEL_ID}\\n{adapter_line}instruction: !include prompts/system.md\\ntools:\\n\"\n    y += \"\".join(f\"  - {t}\\n\" for t in tools)\n    if analyzer:\n        (d / \"sub_agents\").mkdir()\n        (d / \"sub_agents/analyzer.md\").write_text(ANALYZER_PROMPT + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        (d / \"sub_agents/sampling.yaml\").write_text(SAMPLING_YAML, encoding=\"utf-8\")   # local copy: '..' in !include is blocked\n        (d / \"sub_agents/code_analyzer.yaml\").write_text(\n            f\"name: code_analyzer_agent\\ndescription: Read-only analysis that locates the root cause of the reported issue.\\nmodel: {MODEL_ID}\\n\" +\n            (f\"adapter: {LORA_NAME}\\n\" if USE_LORA else \"\") +\n            \"instruction: !include analyzer.md\\ntools:\\n\" + \"\".join(f\"  - {t}\\n\" for t in [\"read_file\"] + GRAPH_TOOLS) +\n            \"generate_content_config: !include sampling.yaml\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        y += \"  - agent_tool:\\n      config_path: sub_agents/code_analyzer.yaml\\n      skip_summarization: true\\n\"\n    y += \"generate_content_config: !include configs/sampling.yaml\\n\"\n    (d / \"agent.yaml\").write_text(y, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    return d\n\nARMS = {\n    \"M0_minimal\": write_arm(\"M0_minimal\", MINIMAL_PROMPT),\n    \"L1_lean\": write_arm(\"L1_lean\", LEAN_PROMPT),\n    \"L2_lean_analyzer\": write_arm(\"L2_lean_analyzer\", LEAN_PROMPT + \"\\nYou may delegate localization to the code_analyzer tool; it returns a short report. Verify its claim by reading the cited lines before editing.\\n\", analyzer=True),\n}\nif USE_LORA:\n    ARMS[\"L3_analyzer_lora\"] = write_arm(\n        \"L3_analyzer_lora\",\n        LEAN_PROMPT + \"\\\\nDelegate localization when useful, then verify cited source lines before editing.\\\\n\",\n        analyzer=True\n    )\n\nprint(\"budget used in every arm:\", BUDGET, \"|\", BUDGET_SOURCE)\nfor n, d in ARMS.items():\n    print(f\"{n:18s}\", sorted(str(p.relative_to(d)) for p in d.rglob(\"*\") if p.is_file()))\nprint(\"\\n--- L1_lean/agent.yaml ---\\n\" + (ARMS[\"L1_lean\"] / \"agent.yaml\").read_text())","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-07T04:55:51.399016Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-07T04:55:51.399464Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-07T04:55:51.464681Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-07T04:55:51.399405Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-07T04:55:51.463333Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"budget used in every arm: {'max_tool_calls': 10, 'max_time_minutes': 1, 'max_turns': 50, 'timeout_seconds': 60} | mirrored from sample_submission/eval_config.yaml\nM0_minimal         ['agent.yaml', 'configs/sampling.yaml', 'eval_config.yaml', 'prompts/system.md']\nL1_lean            ['agent.yaml', 'configs/sampling.yaml', 'eval_config.yaml', 'prompts/system.md']\nL2_lean_analyzer   ['agent.yaml', 'configs/sampling.yaml', 'eval_config.yaml', 'prompts/system.md', 'sub_agents/analyzer.md', 'sub_agents/code_analyzer.yaml', 'sub_agents/sampling.yaml']\n\n--- L1_lean/agent.yaml ---\nname: l1_lean\nmodel: gemma-4-31b-it-qat-w4a16-ct\ninstruction: !include prompts/system.md\ntools:\n  - run_command\n  - read_file\n  - edit_file\n  - write_file\n  - get_status\n  - submit_patch\n  - get_code_neighbors\n  - search_similar_code\n  - get_code_subgraph\ngenerate_content_config: !include configs/sampling.yaml\n\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":10},{"id":"b23d2abc","cell_type":"code","source":"# 6a. Structural validator. Offline approximation of the README rules; NOT a substitute for the official validator.\nALLOWED_EXT = {\".yaml\", \".yml\", \".md\", \".txt\", \".py\", \".json\", \".safetensors\"}\nMAX_UNPACKED = 3 * 1024**3\n\ndef validate_submission(d):\n    d, errs = Path(d).resolve(), []\n    roots = [n for n in (\"agent.yaml\", \"agent.yml\", \"root_agent.yaml\", \"root_agent.yml\") if (d / n).exists()]\n    if len(roots) != 1:\n        errs.append(f\"need exactly one root config, found {roots}\")\n    total, models, adapters = 0, set(), set()\n    for p in d.rglob(\"*\"):\n        if p.is_symlink():\n            errs.append(f\"symlink: {p.name}\")\n        if p.is_file():\n            total += p.stat().st_size\n            if p.suffix.lower() not in ALLOWED_EXT:\n                errs.append(f\"extension not allowed: {p.name}\")\n    if total > MAX_UNPACKED:\n        errs.append(\"unpacked size above 3 GiB\")\n    for y in d.rglob(\"*.yaml\"):\n        txt = y.read_text(errors=\"replace\")\n        models |= {m.group(1).split(\"/\")[-1] for m in re.finditer(r\"^\\s*model:\\s*(\\S+)\", txt, re.M)}\n        adapters |= {m.group(1) for m in re.finditer(r\"^\\s*adapter:\\s*(\\S+)\", txt, re.M)}\n        for m in re.finditer(r\"!include\\s+(\\S+)\", txt):\n            tgt = (y.parent / m.group(1)).resolve()\n            if \"..\" in m.group(1) or d not in tgt.parents or not tgt.exists():\n                errs.append(f\"{y.name}: bad include {m.group(1)}\")\n        for m in re.finditer(r\"config_path:\\s*(\\S+)\", txt):\n            if not (d / m.group(1)).exists():\n                errs.append(f\"{y.name}: config_path missing {m.group(1)}\")\n    if models != {MODEL_ID}:\n        errs.append(f\"expected exactly one base model {MODEL_ID}, found {sorted(models)}\")\n    for a in adapters:\n        if not ((d / \"adapters\" / a / \"adapter_config.json\").exists() and (d / \"adapters\" / a / \"adapter_model.safetensors\").exists()):\n            errs.append(f\"adapter '{a}' referenced but folder incomplete\")\n    for md_file in d.rglob(\"*.md\"):\n        if re.search(r\"\\{[a-zA-Z_]+\\}\", md_file.read_text(errors=\"replace\")):\n            errs.append(f\"{md_file.name}: contains an unfilled {{placeholder}}\")\n    # every declared tool must be a name the harness is known to provide\n    known = set(BASE_TOOLS + GRAPH_TOOLS)\n    for m in re.finditer(r\"^\\s+-\\s+([a-z_]+)\\s*$\", (d / \"agent.yaml\").read_text() if (d / \"agent.yaml\").exists() else \"\", re.M):\n        if m.group(1) not in known:\n            errs.append(f\"unknown tool: {m.group(1)}\")\n    return errs\n\nfor n, d in ARMS.items():\n    e = validate_submission(d)\n    print(f\"{n:18s}\", \"OK\" if not e else e)\n    assert not e, e","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-07T04:55:51.467374Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-07T04:55:51.467893Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-07T04:55:51.494175Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-07T04:55:51.467854Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-07T04:55:51.492674Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"M0_minimal         OK\nL1_lean            OK\nL2_lean_analyzer   OK\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":11},{"id":"51a15ff0","cell_type":"code","source":"# 6b. Package. ZIP root must contain agent.yaml (not a parent folder). Default candidate = L1_lean until section 8 says otherwise.\ndef make_zip(src_dir, out_path):\n    src_dir, out_path = Path(src_dir), Path(out_path)\n    if out_path.exists():\n        out_path.unlink()\n    with zipfile.ZipFile(out_path, \"w\", zipfile.ZIP_DEFLATED, compresslevel=6) as z:\n        for p in sorted(src_dir.rglob(\"*\")):\n            if p.is_file():\n                z.write(p, p.relative_to(src_dir).as_posix())\n    with zipfile.ZipFile(out_path) as z:\n        names = z.namelist()\n        assert \"agent.yaml\" in names, \"agent.yaml must be at the ZIP root\"\n        assert len(names) == len(set(names)), \"duplicate ZIP entries\"\n        assert not any(n.startswith(\"/\") or \"..\" in n.split(\"/\") for n in names)\n    return names\n\nDEFAULT_ARM = \"L1_lean\"\nZIP_PATH = WORK / \"submission.zip\"\nnames = make_zip(ARMS[DEFAULT_ARM], ZIP_PATH)\nprint(f\"{ZIP_PATH}  ({ZIP_PATH.stat().st_size/1024:.1f} KiB)  arm={DEFAULT_ARM}\")\nprint(\"\\n\".join(\"  \" + n for n in names))\nprint(\"\\nA valid submission.zip now exists. Sections 7-9 only decide whether a more complex arm should replace it.\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-07T04:55:51.495739Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-07T04:55:51.496424Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-07T04:55:51.543686Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-07T04:55:51.496372Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-07T04:55:51.541975Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"/kaggle/working/submission.zip  (2.4 KiB)  arm=L1_lean\n  agent.yaml\n  configs/sampling.yaml\n  eval_config.yaml\n  prompts/system.md\n\nA valid submission.zip now exists. Sections 7-9 only decide whether a more complex arm should replace it.\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":12},{"id":"264086a2","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 7. Official-harness evaluation (optional; needs Docker + `swegemma`)\n\nRules enforced here, all learned from the earlier notebooks' failed runs:\n- The **official sample submission runs first** as a gate. If it cannot complete cleanly, nothing else is run, because the problem is the environment, not the agents.\n- A run is **VALID** only if every selected task has exactly one outcome, the harness exited 0, and there are no Docker/sandbox/infrastructure signatures. Infra failures are never counted as unresolved tasks.\n- All arms use the same task IDs, budgets, model and sandbox. CLI flags are checked against `swegemma eval --help` before use.\n- Default is a small **screen** (preliminary only). Set `GEMMA_EVAL_MODE=full` for all tasks.","metadata":{}},{"id":"7231b419","cell_type":"code","source":"# 7a. Harness helpers\nEVAL_MODE = os.environ.get(\"GEMMA_EVAL_MODE\", \"screen\")            # screen | full\nSCREEN_N = int(os.environ.get(\"GEMMA_SCREEN_N\", \"8\"))\nSANDBOX = os.environ.get(\"GEMMA_SANDBOX\", \"docker\")\nCONCURRENCY = int(os.environ.get(\"GEMMA_CONCURRENCY\", \"1\"))\nARM_TIMEOUT_MIN = int(os.environ.get(\"GEMMA_ARM_TIMEOUT_MIN\", \"240\"))\nRUN_ID = time.strftime(\"%Y%m%dT%H%M%S\", time.gmtime())\n\nINFRA_SIGS = (\"error while fetching server api version\", \"cannot connect to the docker\", \"docker daemon\",\n              \"docker.errors\", \"connection refused\", \"failed to start sandbox\", \"sandbox launch\", \"no such container\",\n              \"vllm server\", \"server failed to start\")\nRESOLVED_KEYS = (\"resolved\", \"is_resolved\", \"passed\", \"success\", \"pass\")\nID_KEYS = (\"instance_id\", \"task_id\", \"id\")\n\ndef select_task_ids(tasks, n, seed=SEED):\n    by = defaultdict(list)\n    for t in tasks:\n        by[t.get(\"repo\")].append(t[\"instance_id\"])\n    rng = random.Random(seed)\n    for v in by.values():\n        rng.shuffle(v)\n    order, repos = [], sorted(by)\n    while any(by.values()) and (n is None or len(order) < n):\n        for r in repos:\n            if by[r] and (n is None or len(order) < n):\n                order.append(by[r].pop())\n    return order\n\ndef supported_flags():\n    rc, out = sh([SWEGEMMA, \"eval\", \"--help\"], timeout=60)\n    return set(re.findall(r\"--[a-z][a-z0-9-]+\", out)) if rc == 0 else set()\n\ndef run_arm(label, sub_dir, task_ids, run_root):\n    res = Path(run_root) / label\n    shutil.rmtree(res, ignore_errors=True)\n    res.mkdir(parents=True)\n    flags = supported_flags()\n    wanted = [(\"--tasks\", str(TASKS_PATH)), (\"--snapshots-dir\", str(SNAPSHOTS)), (\"--submission-dir\", str(sub_dir)),\n              (\"--results-dir\", str(res)), (\"--sandbox\", SANDBOX),\n              (\"--max-tool-calls\", str(BUDGET[\"max_tool_calls\"])), (\"--max-time-minutes\", str(BUDGET[\"max_time_minutes\"])),\n              (\"--timeout-seconds\", str(BUDGET[\"timeout_seconds\"])), (\"--verification-timeout-seconds\", str(BUDGET[\"timeout_seconds\"])),\n              (\"--concurrency\", str(CONCURRENCY))]\n    cmd = [SWEGEMMA, \"eval\"]\n    REQUIRED = {\"--tasks\", \"--snapshots-dir\", \"--submission-dir\", \"--results-dir\"}\n    for k, v in wanted:\n        if not flags or k in flags:\n            cmd += [k, v]\n        elif k in REQUIRED:\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"installed swegemma does not list required flag {k}; check `swegemma eval --help`\")\n        else:\n            print(f\"  (optional flag {k} not supported by this swegemma; omitted)\")\n    if \"--task-ids\" in flags:\n        cmd += [\"--task-ids\", *task_ids]\n    elif \"--task-id\" in flags and len(task_ids) == 1:\n        cmd += [\"--task-id\", task_ids[0]]\n    else:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Installed swegemma CLI does not expose --task-ids; use the competition-compatible version.\")\n    t0 = time.time()\n    try:\n        with open(res / \"stdout.log\", \"w\") as lf:\n            p = subprocess.run(cmd, stdout=lf, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, text=True, timeout=ARM_TIMEOUT_MIN * 60)\n        rc = p.returncode\n    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:\n        rc = -9\n    return dict(label=label, dir=res, returncode=rc, elapsed=round(time.time() - t0, 1), cmd=\" \".join(cmd))\n\ndef _row_outcome(row):\n    blob = json.dumps(row, default=str).lower()\n    infra = next((s for s in INFRA_SIGS if s in blob), None)\n    for k in RESOLVED_KEYS:\n        if k in row and isinstance(row[k], (bool, int)):\n            return bool(row[k]), infra\n    status = str(row.get(\"status\", row.get(\"outcome\", \"\"))).lower()\n    if status in (\"resolved\", \"pass\", \"passed\", \"success\"):\n        return True, infra\n    if status in (\"unresolved\", \"fail\", \"failed\", \"failure\") and not infra:\n        return False, infra\n    return None, infra\n\ndef parse_run(info, expected_ids):\n    d = info[\"dir\"]\n    outcomes, infra_reasons, unknown = {}, [], []\n    tr = d / \"task_results.jsonl\"\n    rows = []\n    if tr.exists():\n        for line in tr.read_text().splitlines():\n            if line.strip():\n                try:\n                    rows.append(json.loads(line))\n                except Exception:\n                    pass\n    for r in rows:\n        tid = next((r[k] for k in ID_KEYS if k in r), None)\n        res, infra = _row_outcome(r)\n        if infra:\n            infra_reasons.append(f\"{tid}: {infra}\")\n        if res is None:\n            unknown.append(tid)\n        elif tid is not None and not infra:\n            outcomes[tid] = res\n    log = (d / \"stdout.log\").read_text(errors=\"replace\").lower() if (d / \"stdout.log\").exists() else \"\"\n    log_sig = next((s for s in INFRA_SIGS if s in log), None)\n    ids = [next((r[k] for k in ID_KEYS if k in r), None) for r in rows]\n    dup = [i for i, c in Counter(ids).items() if c > 1]\n    missing = sorted(set(expected_ids) - set(ids))\n    reasons = []\n    if info[\"returncode\"] != 0: reasons.append(f\"harness exit code {info['returncode']}\")\n    if infra_reasons: reasons.append(f\"infra signatures in {len(infra_reasons)} task rows, e.g. {infra_reasons[0]}\")\n    if log_sig and not outcomes: reasons.append(f\"infra signature in stdout.log: {log_sig}\")\n    if missing: reasons.append(f\"missing task ids: {missing[:5]}\")\n    if dup: reasons.append(f\"duplicate task ids: {dup[:5]}\")\n    if unknown: reasons.append(f\"unknown outcomes: {len(unknown)} (inspect task_results.jsonl keys)\")\n    valid = not reasons and len(outcomes) == len(expected_ids)\n    return dict(label=info[\"label\"], valid=valid, reasons=reasons, outcomes=outcomes,\n                resolved=sum(outcomes.values()) if valid else None, n=len(expected_ids), elapsed=info[\"elapsed\"])\n\ndef mcnemar_exact(cand, base):\n    ids = sorted(set(cand) & set(base))\n    b = sum(cand[i] and not base[i] for i in ids)      # candidate wins\n    c = sum(base[i] and not cand[i] for i in ids)      # candidate losses\n    n = b + c\n    p = 1.0 if n == 0 else min(1.0, 2 * sum(math.comb(n, k) for k in range(0, min(b, c) + 1)) / 2**n)\n    return dict(n_pairs=len(ids), wins=b, losses=c, ties=len(ids) - n, p_exact=round(p, 4))\nprint(\"harness helpers ready | mode:\", EVAL_MODE, \"| sandbox:\", SANDBOX)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-07T04:55:51.546413Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-07T04:55:51.548816Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-07T04:55:51.582707Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-07T04:55:51.548777Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-07T04:55:51.581305Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"harness helpers ready | mode: screen | sandbox: docker\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":13},{"id":"f6c0a213","cell_type":"code","source":"# 7b. Run: gate first, then arms. Skipped with a clear message if the environment cannot support it.\nRUNS = {}\nif not CAN_RUN_HARNESS:\n    print(\"SKIPPED: harness evaluation unavailable (need swegemma CLI, a reachable Docker daemon, tasks, snapshots, sample_submission).\")\n    print(\"The default L1_lean submission.zip from section 6 stays as the candidate. No performance claim is made.\")\nelse:\n    ids = select_task_ids(TASKS, SCREEN_N if EVAL_MODE == \"screen\" else None)\n    run_root = RESULTS_DIR / RUN_ID\n    print(f\"{len(ids)} tasks ({EVAL_MODE}); budgets {BUDGET}; sandbox {SANDBOX}\")\n    gate = parse_run(run_arm(\"G_official_sample\", SAMPLE_SUB, ids, run_root), ids)\n    RUNS[\"G_official_sample\"] = gate\n    print(\"gate:\", \"VALID\" if gate[\"valid\"] else f\"INVALID -> {gate['reasons']}\")\n    if not gate[\"valid\"]:\n        print(\"STOP: the official sample did not run cleanly, so this is an environment problem. Fix it before comparing agents.\")\n    else:\n        print(f\"  official sample resolved {gate['resolved']}/{gate['n']} in {gate['elapsed']}s\")\n        candidate_names = [\"L1_lean\", \"L2_lean_analyzer\", \"M0_minimal\"]\n        if \"L3_analyzer_lora\" in ARMS:\n            candidate_names.append(\"L3_analyzer_lora\")\n        for name in candidate_names:\n            RUNS[name] = parse_run(run_arm(name, ARMS[name], ids, run_root), ids)\n            r = RUNS[name]\n            print(f\"  {name:18s}\", f\"resolved {r['resolved']}/{r['n']} in {r['elapsed']}s\" if r[\"valid\"] else f\"INVALID {r['reasons']}\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-07T04:55:51.58414Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-07T04:55:51.584575Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-07T04:55:51.613628Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-07T04:55:51.584534Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-07T04:55:51.612584Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"SKIPPED: harness evaluation unavailable (need swegemma CLI, a reachable Docker daemon, tasks, snapshots, sample_submission).\nThe default L1_lean submission.zip from section 6 stays as the candidate. No performance claim is made.\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":14},{"id":"7b86d6b8","cell_type":"code","source":"# 8. Compare and decide which arm to ship. Default stays L1_lean unless the evidence is clear.\nDECISION_MIN_GAIN = 2        # an arm must resolve at least this many more tasks than L1_lean on a valid run\nDECISION_MIN_TASKS = 20      # smaller screens are preliminary and never change the default\nCHOSEN = DEFAULT_ARM\ndecision_note = \"no valid harness comparison available; keeping default\"\nvalid = {k: v for k, v in RUNS.items() if v[\"valid\"]}\nif \"L1_lean\" in valid:\n    base = valid[\"L1_lean\"]\n    print(f\"{'arm':20s}{'resolved':>10s}{'wins':>6